  "description": "XOWPEI crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C58 H72 Br4 N4 Nd4 O30 Zn2,2(C2 H6 O1),2(C2 H3 N1). From the CIF bond table, Nd1 (Nd) has 8 O neighbors; Nd2 (Nd) has 9 O neighbors; Zn1 (Zn) has 4 O neighbors; Nd3 (Nd) has 8 O neighbors; Nd4 (Nd) has 9 O neighbors; Zn2 (Zn) has 4 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 9 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.462-4.216 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 97.73-128.45°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C66H88Br4N6Nd4O32Zn2.",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
